<code>assert \forall String w; w != null && word.startsWith(w); this.keysWithPrefix(w).contains(word);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall String w; w != null && this.startsWith(w); this.keysWithPrefix(w).contains(word);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall String w; w != null && word.startsWith(w); this.keysWithPrefix(w).contains(word);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall String w; w != null && this.startsWith(w); \result.contains(word));</code>

However, the above assert statement is not entirely correct because `\result` refers to the return value of the `add` method, which is a boolean, not a list of strings. We need to use the `keysWithPrefix` method to check the condition. Here's the corrected version:

<code>assert \forall String w; w != null && this.startsWith(w); this.keysWithPrefix(w).contains(word));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall String w; w != null && word.startsWith(w); this.keysWithPrefix(w).contains(word);</code>
--------------------
